From 10542ac3c86065693f6c0b3c8ec814fa1d2aad98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NEMO Rung5 <nemo-dev@localhost>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:06:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Rung 5b retracted: type-50 Jacobian verified entry-exact;
 two-legged gate

A read-only diagnosis and an exhaustive per-reaction-analytic sweep show the
type-50 (ice-transport + grain-grain) Jacobian in get_jacobian is already
entry-exact. The Rung-5-era "021 != 022 on type-50 rows, blocked on Rung 5b"
finding was a finite-difference cancellation artifact in the oracle, not a
Jacobian gap. Rung 5b is retracted -- there is nothing to complete.

Why the gain entries were already correct: ice transport carries the collision
partner GRAIN_j as an explicit reactant, so the reactant differentiator visits
the reaction and deposits d(flux)/dY(GRAIN_j) to every product bin, including the
redistributed non-reactant bins. This is unlike the Rung-4 live divisor, where
the grain entered only through a rate coefficient with no compound to trigger the
column. The gain-side-gap hypothesis was therefore wrong.

Exhaustive proof (tests/ice_transport_jac_sweep.{f90,sh}, committed as the
standing type-50 gate leg): get_jacobian isolated to type-50 vs an independent
hand-summed per-reaction analytic derivative of the RHS flux, every column, every
row, light (ice 1e-10) and heavy (ice 1e-8) states -> 393 nonzero entries per
state, 786 comparisons, 0 mismatches, agreement at machine epsilon (max rel
2.3e-16). Ten subset-FD anchors (ice transport + grain-grain, bins 2/3/4, both
charge columns) confirm the analytic model against a background-free finite
difference. Characterization tool retained (tests/ice_transport_jac_diag.{f90,sh}).

General lesson recorded (docs/PhaseII_rung5_site_classification.md sec 4.4): FD
Jacobian verification has a noise floor at ~1e-5 of the background derivative --
a coupling smaller than that (J03CH2OH<->GRAIN01 is ~6e-6 of its chemistry
background; GRAIN02<->GRAIN01 ~2e-5 of its coag background) is lost to
cancellation when the RHS is differenced. The equivalence gate is now two-legged:
FD above the floor (the Rung-5 chemistry entries, which dominate the rows they
touch), per-reaction-analytic below it (the type-50 entries).

Production mf stays 121 pending the Rung 5c convergence test (021 vs 121 in a
bin-depleting regime); the retarget to 021 is decided on that evidence, not on
any remaining analytic work.
